# WaySlice ignore rules
# Order: dot-prefixed folders -> specs -> devlog -> dev scripts -> screenshot sources
# -> prompt reference -> sample tracks -> dependencies

# -- 1. Dot-prefixed folders (local tooling artifacts, not committed) --
# Currently matches: .playwright-mcp/ (browser test artifacts), .workbuddy/, etc.
# This rule does not affect the .gitignore file itself (it is not a folder).
# To commit a dot folder in the future (e.g. .github/), add an explicit
# un-ignore line after this rule, e.g.:
# !.github/
.*/

# -- 2. Specs and task notes --
/specs/

# -- 3. Dev log --
/devlog/

# -- 4. Dev and build scripts --
# Nothing in the web runtime depends on them (verified with a browser network
# log: load, upload, sectoring and export make zero /tools requests), and the
# READMEs no longer mention them. Local dev tooling only (icon build, sample
# track generation, syntax checks).
/tools/

# -- 5. Screenshot source files --
# Raw phone screenshots and per-image PNG versions, used only to generate the
# published .jpg files in the parent directory, locally. The web runtime never
# requests them: the READMEs reference /screenshots/*.jpg and the sibling
# overview.jpg (repo-wide search confirmed nothing references this folder).
/screenshots/png/

# -- 6. Prompt reference material --
# prompt/ is local reference material only; the web runtime never requests it.
# The READMEs' build-your-own section was removed and no longer mentions it.
/prompt/

# -- 7. Sample tracks --
# Sample GPX files are for local manual testing only (loaded through the
# browser file picker); the web runtime never requests them.
/sample/

# -- 8. Dependencies --
# Dev dependencies (Playwright etc.); the web runtime does not depend on them.
/node_modules/
